# Commit the shared project skill tree (Claude Code's documented location).
# The rest of the developer-local root .claude/ stays ignored. Anchored to the
# repo root so the nested example-pack .claude/ rules above are untouched.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/

# ...but NOT the machine-local sink `gc prime` materializes inside it
# (gc-em7gg). Those entries are absolute symlinks embedding a content-addressed
# pack-cache hash, e.g.
#   core.gc-work -> /Users/<user>/.gc/cache/repos/<64-hex>/internal/bootstrap/
#                   packs/core/skills/gc-work
# so they are meaningless in any other checkout and all of them flip together
# whenever the pack cache hash changes. Measured 2026-09-06: `git add -A --
# dry-run -- .claude` staged eight such entries in this repo, which is the
# worst case of this class because the parent directory is deliberately
# TRACKED (the shared gascity-docs skill tree lives here and must stay).
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the generated names, so gascity-docs/ and any
# future hand-authored skill remain tracked.
/.claude/skills/core.*
/.claude/skills/.gc-skill-ownership.json

# sync-project-agents writes local migration backups here; don't commit them.
.agents/migration/
.gc/

